gary you talk straight  how are you feeling after last night did  the best team win  best team won uh if we look at it just  purely on football absolutely they  played a really good game in italy after  a difficult start the game they  they got on top they controlled the game  demonstrated authority in the class that  they have they've obviously got a  fantastic goalkeeper they've got a  defense that's  resilient and they've got a an unbeaten  record now which i think stretches back  some 30 odd matches so look in the end  we just couldn't go that sort of extra  and go over that extra hurdle but how do  i feel this morning  i feel i feel quite good um in the sense  of  as an england fan and watching the  players and thinking about how they've  handled this tournament good about our  manager good about the way in which the  players conducted themselves the way it  wished to perform  you know gareth and the players found a  way to get to that final last night  i know people will say that maybe we  could have been this or we could have  been that could be more attacking could  have made that substitution all those  things that were here but they got  it so right during this tournament that  i trusted them to the end and they just  fell  short uh but proud proud of the players  proud of everything that they've  achieved uh i feel connected to them  i've not always felt connected to  england teams as a fan growing up and  even as sometimes a player and as a  coach but i felt connected to this team  because i felt as though they did  everything in a way in which to be fair  you should they carried themselves  brilliantly on and off the pitch  and they played really well uh  you've been there you've suffered this  kind of defeat and disappointment with  england yourself as a player  give us an insight into how that team  will be feeling this morning especially  those three young players i mean  the youngest sucker just 19 missing  those  penalty spot kicks how will they be  feeling this morning and what will gary  southgate  be doing to look after them honestly  there'll be none some of them obviously  the ones who may be feeling a little bit  more than the others the ones who maybe  miss the penalty or not they'll be sad  but they'll want to go away with the  families they want to take some time off  they need a mental and physical break  that'll be there for  their first thought how quickly can they  get on a plane and get somewhere whereby  they can just relax and reset  and think about starting again in a few  weeks time but obviously as well they'll  have that many words sort of coming  at them they'll just want silence i  always wanted when i went out of a  tournament i just always wanted to get  away as quickly as possible really  and just to be on my own with the family  not talking about football just getting  back to normality because they've been  in a bubble for the last five six  seven weeks not been able to see the  families not being able to  obviously mix with anybody they'll have  been in that hotel room  and they'll just want basically  normality back in their lives for a few  weeks they've done it  incredibly well the spotlight and  scrutiny has been on them  um and they've been heavily praised for  everything that they've done in this  last few weeks but they'll just want  some peace and quiet in their lives this  morning if it was like  you know when i got knocked out of the  tournament but they should also be  incredibly proud of everything that  and everything that they've achieved as  well because they've done they've done  something no england team has done for  55 years that's reaching a final i know  it's not enough  because we had to win to really take it  that step further but it's still  brilliant what they've achieved in the  in these last few weeks  gary you do hope that the players do  switch off in a sense because  if some of them look at social media  this morning  it will make for awful reading  a 